## Summary

**Screens & components annotated** (14 files, 165 hinted elements):

- **Dashboard** — `dashboard.create` (+ `.empty` suffix for the empty-state duplicate), `dashboard.search` (input, `controls=dashboard.resumes`), `dashboard.sort` (select with `data-semtag-options` + `dashboard.sort.option.*`), `dashboard.resumes` collection, `dashboard.empty-message`.
- **ResumeCard** — items keyed by `resume.id`: title `dashboard.resumes.item.<id>` (navigation → `editor.screen`), `.updated`, `.template` observables, `.menu`/`.rename`/`.duplicate`/`.delete` actions, and scoped rename/delete dialog regions with `.title`, `.cancel`, `.save`/`.confirm`.
- **Editor shell** — `editor.back`, `editor.title` / `editor.title.input` (mutually exclusive), `editor.preview.toggle` (toggle, `controls=editor.preview`), `editor.tabs` collection with `editor.tabs.item.<tab>` navigation, one region per tab panel (`editor.contact` … `editor.sections`), `editor.preview` region.
- **Forms** — Contact inputs (`editor.contact.*` ↔ state `contact.*`), Summary textarea + char counter, Experience/Education as collections keyed by entry id with per-item inputs and `.move-up`/`.move-down`/`.remove`, Skills (add-region, level selects with options, chip collection), TemplateSelector (`editor.template.item.<style>` as `option` with literal `selected` state), SectionManager (`editor.sections.item.<type>` with `.title`, `.visible`, move actions; state keys `section.<type>.title|visible`).
- **Preview** (all 3 templates) — shared `preview.*` namespace: contact observables, section headings (state `section.<type>.title`), `preview.experience.list` / `preview.education.list` / `preview.skills.list` collections, per-item observables. Same state keys as the editor inputs, so the agent can connect a field edit to its preview rendering.
- **NotFound** — `notfound.message`, `notfound.home`.

**Validator:** 0 errors. 15 warnings, all `duplicate-id` across the three preview templates — intentional: `ResumePreview` renders exactly one template (a `switch`), so `preview.*` ids are unique at runtime, and sharing them keeps agent selectors stable when the template changes. ClassicTemplate renders skills as one joined string, so it has `preview.skills.text` instead of a foldable list — the one collection that can't fold there.

**Known limitation:** dropdown/select/dialog content is Radix-portaled, so those per-item controls won't sit under the `dashboard.resumes` collection ancestor in the DOM and won't fold into its block — but only one is ever open, so the snapshot cost is one expanded entry. Left unhinted: decorative icons, layout wrappers, the app logo, and the unused `NavLink.tsx`.

